<title>HONG KONG: Emperor Int'l interim profit up 28.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Emperor Int'l interim profit up 28.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   22.40     vs 17.38</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.8	 vs 1.8</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  5.66 loss vs 2.40 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    81.46     vs 63.21</p>
<p>    Turnover		     850.84    vs 946.23</p>
<p>    Company name		 Emperor International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  February 12 to March 13</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   March 18</p>
<p>NOTE - Emperor International Holdings is a property investment company.</p>
<p>Exceptional loss represents amortisation of premium on redemption of convertible notes and provision for advances and accrued interest receivable due from a director of a subsidiary.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
